      },
      "worked": "The top row gives the common sum:\n$$2-5+0=-3.$$\nUse the diagonal containing $2$ and $-4$ to find the centre:\n$$\\begin{align*}-3-2-(-4)&=-3-2+4\\\\&=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nThe other diagonal gives the bottom-left entry:\n$$\\begin{align*}-3-0-(-1)&=-3+1\\\\&=-2.\\end{align*}$$\nComplete the bottom row:\n$$\\begin{align*}-3-(-2)-(-4)&=-3+2+4\\\\&=3.\\end{align*}$$\nComplete the left column:\n$$\\begin{align*}-3-2-(-2)&=-3-2+2\\\\&=-3.\\end{align*}$$\nComplete the right column:\n$$\\begin{align*}-3-0-(-4)&=-3+4\\\\&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nThe completed rows are $(2,-5,0)$, $(-3,-1,1)$ and $(-2,3,-4)$. Every row, column and diagonal sums to $-3$.",
